{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>That your days may multiply.</b> It is difficult: why did it not place this statement before the statement ״וּכְתַבְתָּם,״ so that the statement ״וּכְתַבְתָּם״ would refer back also to the verse ״לְמַעַן יִרְבּוּ״? Or perhaps it intended to juxtapose the statement ״לְמַעַן יִרְבּוּ״ to the statement ״וּכְתַבְתָּם,״ to say that in the merit of ״וּכְתַבְתָּם״ your days shall multiply — and this is their statement, of blessed memory (Shabbat 32a): whoever is meticulous in the mitzvah of mezuzah, his days and years are lengthened for him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:35.555923848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}